; bfsodium KEYGEN : the Poly1305 one time key  RFC 8439 section 2 point 6
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The block function is PASTED from its own verified
; file; what is here is the placement of the forty four bytes it works from and
; the truncation of its answer  and nothing else;
;
; INTERFACE entry=63 exit=0 footprint=0:271
; IO  in:  key{32}  nonce{12}     (44 bytes)
;     out: otk{32}                (32 bytes)
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x10f  the block routine's whole frame; blockloop runs HERE at this
;                 file's own zero and its footprint 0:271 is what sets the size
;                 of it; the forty eight bytes it works from go in at
;                 @0x010:0x03f and the keystream comes back at @0x000:0x03f
;   @0x010:0x02f  key{32}    u8  the ChaCha20 key
;   @0x030:0x033  ctr{4} LE  u8  the block counter; NEVER WRITTEN  so it stays
;                 nought  which is exactly what section 2 point 6 asks for; the
;                 read prologue steps over these four cells rather than filling
;                 them  and the contract below is what says they are still clear
;   @0x034:0x03f  nonce{12}  u8
;
; The one time key is the first thirty two bytes of the block that the counter
; nought produces; the second thirty two are discarded  which is the whole of
; the difference between this and the block function itself; The AEAD calls
; this once  before it encrypts anything  because encryption starts at counter
; one and must not reuse the block this consumed;

; read the key  step over the counter  then read the nonce
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>>>>>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=+63
; to the block routine's base  which is where a paste site always stands
L63
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; the counter was stepped over and not written  so it is still nought
; ASSERT zero +48:+51
; and nothing above the forty eight input bytes has been touched
; ASSERT zero +64:+271
@@BLOCK@@ 0
; ASSERT ptr=+0

; emit
; the one time key  the first thirty two bytes of the block
  .>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.>.
